title: 'Cancellation: stop scope + cooperative unwind at suspension points'
status: complete
atomic: true
priority: medium
blocked_by:
- 2-6-3
created_at: '2026-06-13T14:45:40'
updated_at: '2026-06-13T19:23:52'
result: 'Cooperative cancellation implemented. `stop <scope>` cancels a named together
  scope: typer tracks scope names and lowers `stop name` to hir::Stmt::ScopeCancel
  -> MIR __scope_cancel -> jinn_scope_cancel. Channel send/recv park loops are cancellation
  points (check coro->cancelled at loop top and under-lock before parking, closing
  the lost-wakeup race); jinn_chan_wake_coro unparks channel-blocked children on cancel.
  Loop back-edges in scheduler tasks are cancellation points via inject_cancel_checks
  (yield_passes.rs): when the task has defers, the check branches to a synthesized
  cancel.cleanup block that runs defers then returns, so defer runs on cancellation.
  Conformance: stop_scope_cancels_without_drain and defer_runs_on_cancellation pass
  (deterministic via a ready-channel handshake); full concurrency_shutdown suite 16/16
  green; lib 249, access_semantics 11, std_stable_subset 2 all pass; only pre-existing
  column_max/min/sum integration failures remain. Bounded/deferred limits (loop-local
  defers, coroutine-parent join wake) documented in docs/concurrency.md.'
description: 'Implement cooperative cancellation. `stop <scope>` and failing child
  mark scope.cancelled + wake all children. Park loops (channel send/recv, sched yield,
  sleep) check coro->cancelled and return a distinct unwind status; the injected yields
  (task 2-10) and channel parks become cancellation points. Unwind reuses early-return
  path: run defers + Perceus drops, return. Cancelled actors skip drain (close + cancel
  flag -> exit at next receive). DoD: stop_scope_cancels_without_drain, defer_runs_on_cancellation
  tests pass. If full unwind-codegen integration with Perceus proves too invasive,
  implement the runtime+park-point flagging and a bounded best-effort unwind, and
  document precisely what is deferred.'
